From 934d2d6e8d849f6f613770646033af171b4223a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:00:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Qwen4Exp: host copies of decode tokens for the PLE n-gram
 hash

The n-gram (PLE) embedding hashes token ids on the host. Every decode step it read
the input ids and the last context tokens (stored in the GDN state slot) back from
the device, two host syncs before the first layer could be launched, which kept the
first pipeline stage's device idle.

The runner already holds both on the host. For decode batches without async
scheduling it now passes the flat input ids and, per row, the last k tokens of the
request's history (k from the model's host_context_tokens, -1 before position 0 and
on padding rows) as two optional attention-metadata fields. Qwen4Exp uses them when
present; prefill and async scheduling keep the device-read path.
QWEN4_PLE_HOST_TOKENS=0 restores the old path, QWEN4_PLE_HOST_CHECK=1 compares both
every step. The H2D copies of the hashed ids are now non-blocking too.

Greedy outputs are unchanged; unit test for the runner helper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
